      "side": 1,
      "message": "My first analysis found the cases, that the install partition differs from `d.installPath` for the files in `system/framework/oat/x86(_64)`, which is the directory that I am installing.\nBut with Jiyong\u0027s comment, I found these cases are only for the files that are not installed. A basename (filename) of the files, for example, is `apex@com.android.btservices@javalib@service-bluetooth.jar@classes.odex` of `service-blutooth` module. These files are not installed to the image.\n\nSo as Jiyong suggested, we may safely use the partition name from `d.installPath`. It also does not change the existing installPath values.",
